  "review_text": "This month had seven graded stories spread over six books, with a final weighted average of [SPAN: severity=error; fontsize=large; fonttype=bold; text=x.xx],\n\n<b>FIXME</b>\n\nmore than a point-and-a-quarter drop from the previous month's <b>5.76</b>,\n\n<b>FIXME</b>\nwith nothing grading higher than 5.5.&nbsp; This was largely due to the two mainline books (ASM and FF) not pulling their weight this time around, submitting lackluster offerings instead, leaving the four anthology-style books flailing by themselves and unable to overcome the lower performances.&nbsp; So sadly, the month as a whole was below reader level.\n\n\n\n[DEVNOTE: *** SUMMARY_BEGIN ***\n*** THIS MONTH ***7 graded stories over 6 issues...TOTAL WEIGHT: 4.75 grade character issue   weight 5.5   ff        FF #20  1.00 5.0   torch     ST #114 0.75 5.0   iron      TOS #47 0.75 4.0   asm       ASM #6  1.00 2.5   giant     TTA #49 0.50 2.0   strange   ST #114 0.25 1.5   thor      JIM #97 0.504.11*** LAST MONTH ***10 graded stories over 9 issues...TOTAL WEIGHT: 8.33 grade character issue       weight 8.0   xmen      XMEN #1     1.00 7.0   ff        FF #19      1.00 6.5   aven      AVEN #1     1.00 6.5   asm       ASM #5      1.00 6.0   ff        FF Annual 1 0.33 5.5   ff        FF Annual 1 2.00 4.5   ant       TTA #48     0.50 4.5   iron      TOS #46     0.50 2.5   thor      JIM #96     0.50 2.5   torch     ST #113     0.505.76\n*** SUMMARY_END ***]",
  "letters_page": "[HANG0] * Introduction of the Lizard, Molecule Man, Lava Man, Living Eraser and Melter\n[HANG0] * Tales of Asgard joining Thor in <i>Journey Into Mystery</i> is a big plus\n[HANG0] * Giant-Man is added to Marvel's ever-growing cast of main characters\n[HANG0] * Captain America try-out in <i>Strange Tales</i>\n\n<b>Roundup:</b>\n[DEVNOTE: *** INTRODUCTION_BEGIN ***\nNotes | first | villain | Lava Man\nNotes | first | Tales of Asgard\nNotes | first | Frost Giants, Fire Giants, Ymir, Surtur\nLiving Eraser | villain | Milestone: (first)\nNotes | first | villain | Supremacy, Ruler of Dimension Z\nLizard | villain | Milestone: (first), (origin)\nNotes | first | Martha Connors\nNotes | first | Billy Connors\nMolecule Man | villain | Milestone: (first), (origin)\nNotes | first | Victoria Bentley\nmelter | villain | Milestone: (first), (origin)\n*** INTRODUCTION_END ***]\n[DEVNOTE: *** HIGHLIGHTS_BEGIN ***]\n[HANG0] * Thor faces a Lava Man, loses Jane, and somehow the romance hurts more than the villain.\n[HANG0] * Giant‑Man arrives on the scene, and the Eraser tries to make sure he doesn't stay long.\n[HANG0] * FIXME - write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME - write something\n[HANG0] * The Human Torch crosses paths with Captain America -- and the story keeps a quiet surprise waiting at the end.\n[HANG0] * Mordo schemes, Strange responds, Victoria steps in -- and the issue still feels like a bookmark waiting for a <i>real</i> story.\n[HANG0] * FIXME - write something\n[DEVNOTE: *** HIGHLIGHTS_END ***]",
  "ownership": "[HANG0] * Both Thor and Giant-Man are up against slippery new menaces\n[HANG0] * An <i>old</i> foe returns to battle Spider-Man\n[HANG0] * While <i>another</i> old enemy looks in on the Human Torch, just not the one he expected...\n[HANG0] * Dr. Strange finally gets an origin tale\n[HANG0] * Colonel Nick Fury visits the FF\n[HANG0] * Iron Man gets a face lift\n[HANG0] * And second outings from both of the new titles <i>Avengers</i> and <i>X-Men</i>."
